&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Environment Test Engineer, you will be responsible for the design, execution, and analysis of environmental stress test campaigns across the full range of drone sub-systems and Ground Support Equipment (GSE). As a generalist within the Environmental Cluster, you will apply your knowledge to mechanical, thermal, and environmental qualification—across multiple hardware domains. The Environmental Cluster is the &quot;Physical Reality&quot; team within the Test Department. Where other clusters validate functionality, the Environmental Cluster validates survivability and performance under real-world stress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The cluster is organized around domain specialists—Launch Systems, Ground Communication Systems—but requires a generalist backbone to ensure test coverage continuity across all sub-systems, absorb campaign overflows from specialist engineers, and extend the cluster&#39;s capability into emerging and sensitive hardware domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The day-to-day&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vibration &amp;amp; Shock Campaigns: Designing and executing vibration test campaigns (sine sweep, random vibration, shock) on drone sub-systems and GSE hardware to simulate transport, operational, and launch-induced dynamic environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thermal Soak &amp;amp; Cycling: Executing controlled thermal exposure tests across the full operational temperature range on any sub-system assigned by the Head of Testing or cluster lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IP &amp;amp; Ingress Testing: Executing dust and water ingress tests on drone enclosures, connectors, and GSE hardware to validate field survivability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Humidity, Salt Spray &amp;amp; Corrosion: Running humidity-controlled and salt-spray campaigns to identify corrosion risks in connectors, structural joints, and electronic housings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Altitude Simulation: Validating component behaviour under simulated low-pressure conditions relevant to the operational altitude range of the drone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fatigue &amp;amp; Endurance: Running high-cycle mechanical campaigns to characterize material and joint fatigue over the required operational life of any assigned sub-system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Failure Mode Boundary Testing: Deliberately pushing hardware beyond its design limits to physically map the failure envelope and validate safety margins across all assigned sub-systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;You’ll-do-great-if-you….3&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;15247&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should apply if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Environmental Standards Literacy: Working knowledge of applicable standards as the primary frameworks for environmental test campaign design and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instrumentation &amp;amp; DAQ: Expert in physical instrumentation—strain gauges, accelerometers, thermocouples, pressure transducers, and load cells. Ability to configure and operate DAQ systems across a wide range of test scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mechanical Systems Understanding: Solid understanding of structural mechanics, material fatigue, vibration dynamics, and shock response for both metallic and composite structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thermal Testing: Experience with thermal chambers, thermal cycling rigs, IR cameras, and thermocouple mapping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Environmental Test Equipment Operation: Hands-on experience operating vibration tables, shock rigs, thermal chambers, IP spray equipment, and salt-spray cabinets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrology: Proficient with precision measurement tools (load frames, calipers, torque meters, dimensional gauges) for pre- and post-test validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic Familiarity with Weapons Hardware Constraints: Understanding of the physical and regulatory constraints that govern the environmental testing of defense-related hardware. Specifically:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of ITAR/EAR export control obligations when handling test data and reports related to lethality hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
